---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Factory & Quality Control"
  description="Brief production framework and quality-control gates for the filter range, with a link to the full factory details on carfilterspro.com."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Factory', href: '/factory/' }]}
>
  <main class="wrap" style="padding-top:2rem;">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Factory</nav>
    <h1>Factory &amp; Quality Control</h1>

    <p class="lede" style="max-width:70ch;">
      This page keeps the production framework concise and product-focused. Detailed factory
      information — facility area, equipment list, staffing and history — lives on the primary
      storefront, not here.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Production process (industry reference)</h2>
      <p>
        Filter manufacturing in the Qinghe cluster typically runs a media-to-finish sequence:
        filter-media production, pleating, frame forming, element assembly and final testing. The
        line descriptions below are drawn from the industry-cluster reference corpus and are{' '}
        <em>not</em> presented as this entity&rsquo;s verified equipment list:
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="data">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Line</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Filter media lines</strong></td><td>Needle-punched and synthetic-fibre media production with lamination.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>HEPA pleating</strong></td><td>Separator and mini-pleat lines using micro-glass media (pleat depths 20–100 mm).</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Frame forming</strong></td><td>Galvanised and stainless frame welding and forming.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Element assembly</strong></td><td>Panel, round, cartridge and pocket element assembly with seal application.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Quality testing</strong></td><td>Efficiency, leakage and pressure-drop test equipment.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Quality-control gates</h2>
      <p>
        Quality control in this industry is organised as a four-gate sequence, described as a
        framework rather than as an audited procedure:
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="data">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Gate</th><th scope="col">What it checks</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>IQC — Incoming</strong></td><td>Raw media, frames, seals and adhesives inspected on receipt against the order specification.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>IPQC — In-process</strong></td><td>Pleat depth, adhesive application and frame dimensions checked during production.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>FQC — Final</strong></td><td>Finished elements tested for efficiency, leakage and pressure drop before release.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>OQC — Outgoing</strong></td><td>Pre-shipment verification of dimensions, packaging, marking and batch documentation.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:0.9rem;">
        HEPA elements are leak-tested before dispatch where a factory leakage-test certificate is
        specified. The{' '}
        <a href={`${site.dataSubsiteUrl}/reference/test-standards/`} rel="noopener" target="_blank">test-standards reference</a>{' '}
        documents the efficiency classifications applied across the range.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Certifications</h2>
      <p class="notice">
        Certifications are not presented until independently verified with certificate numbers. Any
        certification claim seen in third-party catalogues is not attributed to this entity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Full factory details</h2>
      <p class="notice">
        For facility area, equipment, staffing and factory history, see the primary storefront&rsquo;s{' '}
        <a href={site.factoryUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">factory page on carfilterspro.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
